{
"_doc": "World regions. The world scene builds itself from the current region. qi_density multiplies cultivation everywhere in the region (meditation spots multiply again). routes: travel targets with days and an optional min_realm (realm id). places: interactables; 'anchor_id' (optional, globally unique) makes the place a Creation Artifact anchor (data/artifact.json); 'type' picks the script (meditation, merchant, sect_hall, workshop, clinic, orphanage (adopt a foundling, FAM-003e), auction (an auction house: house_id names a data/auctions.json house, AUC-001b), inheritance (inheritance grounds listing every data/inheritances.json inheritance in the region, W-006b), deed_giver, explore, travel, gather, secret_realm: lists every data/secret_realms.json realm whose region is this one; a gather place's gather_table entries are {item ('' = nothing), weight, min, max, min_realm (optional realm id: below it the entry counts as nothing found), seasons (optional list of spring/summer/autumn/winter, SEASON-001: the entry only rolls in those seasons; absent = all year)}), 'pos' and 'size' are in pixels, other keys are passed to the script as exported properties. discovery (optional, TRAV-005): an encounter id (data/encounters.json, marked discovery_only) that your first exploration of this region always finds, once (world flag discovered_<region>). npc_spots (optional): list of [x, y] positions where generated NPCs living in the region stand (in id order; extra NPCs gather around the spawn point). family_home (optional, FAM-011): {pos, size} of the Family Home drawn in the region while any of the player's living spouses or children live there; they take the npc_spots nearest to it. first_visit (optional, TRAV-002): 1-3 sentences posted to the message log the first time the player travels to the region. quiet_lines (optional Array of short non-empty strings) are flavour scenes appended to quiet exploring days, picked by day number (no randomness). encounter_tags select entries from data/encounters.json when exploring. map_pos (optional): [x, y] fractions 0..1 placing the region on the world map screen (regions without it are spread around the map edge). abodes (optional, G-010): claimable cave abodes in the region, each {id (globally unique), display_name, cost (spirit stones), min_realm (optional realm id), qi_density (multiplies cultivation in seclusion there, like a meditation spot), storage_slots (distinct item stacks its chest holds), anchor_id (optional, globally unique: the abode can be bound as a Creation Artifact anchor), pos, size, color (layout for the world scene)}. The player owns at most one abode (Abodes). A merchant's optional 'stock_tags' (item tags it sells and buys back) and 'buy_tags' (item tags it only buys back, e.g. a general trader taking herbs and ore). A merchant's optional 'faction' (sect id) makes its prices follow your reputation with that sect (data/sects.json reputation tiers). encounter_tags select entries from data/encounters.json when exploring. map.ambient (optional, WU-057): particles drifting over the region, {season: kind} with season spring/summer/autumn/winter or any (a season entry wins over any) and kind one of petals, leaves, snow, mist, embers, fireflies (src/world/ambient.gd); the Ambient effects setting turns them off. map.decor (optional): scenery drawn on the map, counts trees/rocks/grass/flowers (0-300) and colors tree_color/rock_color/grass_color/flower_color (hex); missing keys use Scenery.DEFAULTS.",
